@startuml
title GET /api/v1/pods/{pod_id}/stats/players
hide footbox
actor Client
participant "FastAPI / Pydantic" as API
participant "SQLAlchemy session" as DB
database PostgreSQL as PG
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/pods/{pod_id}/stats/players
API -> API: Validate path, query and body
note over API
Invalid input -> 422; access checks also apply.
end note
API -> DB: get_db(): request transaction
ref over API, DB: Clerk identity and route permissions (auth.puml)
DB -> PG: Find pod; missing -> 404
DB -> PG: Aggregate completed appearances, wins and draws by pod_member_id
DB -> PG: Outer join current members, including zero counts
DB -> PG: Order by member ID; apply limit/offset
PG --> DB: Rows / mutation outcome
DB --> API: Route result
API -> API: win_rate = round(100 * wins / games_played, 2)
note over API: Zero appearances -> win_rate 0
API -> API: Validate/serialize response
API -> DB: Finish successful request
DB -> PG: COMMIT
API --> Client: 200
note over API, PG
Any failure aborts the success path and rolls back.
See transaction.puml for shared error handling.
end note
@enduml
